From 45396ad084794a312e815e061c83d682f4a475e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RitzDaCat <49771174+RitzDaCat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] backends/drm: compensate mandatory color pipeline curves

Some DRM color-pipeline graphs contain named transfer functions that cannot be
bypassed. The existing matcher rejects a requested client-to-output pipeline
when such a block appears before or after the programmable operations. On the
tested NVIDIA Full graph, that prevents SDR fullscreen content from using
direct scanout while the output is HDR/WCG.

Program each mandatory named curve and place its mathematical inverse in a
programmable neighbor. Normalize the input of fixed PQ-125 inverse curves in a
preceding matrix so negative minima and linear ranges above 125 are preserved
without clipping. Support a mandatory trailing curve with the inverse folded
into the preceding programmable LUT.

Keep this work outside the frame hot path: successful and failed assignments
continue to use the existing pipeline cache. Add a deterministic mock of the
relevant NVIDIA graph and numerically compare the programmed graph with the
requested transform across its full measured range.

